{"id":"f15t2","name":"Shopping Sessions","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","events_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The product team wants to know how often a visit to our shop ends with a purchase. The website logs every action in <code>events_df</code>, with the columns <code>user_id</code>, <code>ts</code> (timestamp) and <code>event</code> (<code>view</code>, <code>add_to_cart</code> or <code>purchase</code>). Events without a user (visitors who refused cookies) cannot be grouped and are ignored, and the tracker sometimes sends the same event twice (same user, time and event), which counts once.</p>\n<p>We have no notion of visit in the logs, so we build <b>sessions</b>: the events of a user, taken in time order, belong to the same session as long as the gap between two consecutive events is at most 30 minutes; a longer gap starts a new session. A session can last several hours if the user keeps clicking, and it can cross midnight: a session belongs to the day on which it <b>started</b>, even if its purchase happened after midnight. A session is <b>converted</b> if it contains at least one purchase.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per day with at least one session, with the columns <code>day</code> (date), <code>sessions</code> (long), <code>converted</code> (long) and <code>conversion_rate</code> (double, converted sessions divided by sessions, rounded to 3 decimals), sorted by <code>day</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>events_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>ts</th><th>event</th></tr><tr><td>u1</td><td>2026-03-04 10:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>u1</td><td>2026-03-04 10:30:00</td><td>add_to_cart</td></tr><tr><td>u1</td><td>2026-03-04 10:45:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>u1</td><td>2026-03-04 11:16:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>u2</td><td>2026-03-04 23:50:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>u2</td><td>2026-03-05 00:10:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>u3</td><td>2026-03-04 10:10:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>u3</td><td>2026-03-04 10:10:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>null</td><td>2026-03-04 10:20:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>u4</td><td>2026-03-05 08:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>day</th><th>sessions</th><th>converted</th><th>conversion_rate</th></tr><tr><td>2026-03-04</td><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td>2026-03-05</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0.0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, events_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return events_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["consigne longue","sessionisation","lag et somme cumulée","jour de début de session"],"minutes":22,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"events_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"user_id string, ts timestamp, event string","rows":[["u1","2026-03-04 10:00:00","view"],["u1","2026-03-04 10:30:00","add_to_cart"],["u1","2026-03-04 10:45:00","purchase"],["u1","2026-03-04 11:16:00","view"],["u2","2026-03-04 23:50:00","view"],["u2","2026-03-05 00:10:00","purchase"],["u3","2026-03-04 10:10:00","view"],["u3","2026-03-04 10:10:00","view"],[null,"2026-03-04 10:20:00","purchase"],["u4","2026-03-05 08:00:00","view"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["day","sessions","converted","conversion_rate"],"rows":[["2026-03-04",4,2,0.5],["2026-03-05",1,0,0.0]]}},{"input":{"events_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"user_id string, ts timestamp, event string","rows":[["a","2026-03-01 09:00:00","view"],["b","2026-03-01 09:20:00","view"],["a","2026-03-01 09:40:00","purchase"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["day","sessions","converted","conversion_rate"],"rows":[["2026-03-01",3,1,0.333]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}